<h2 id="ha-ctrl-011-acceptance">Acceptance and evidence</h2>

1. Test no target, no records, a Recorder exclusion, purged history and a failed request separately. Never invent zeroes.
2. Change targets and periods quickly. Compare the heading, plot, table and export scope. A late response must not overwrite a newer choice.
3. Compare raw state history with a supported statistic for the same period and label how they differ. Keep signs, gaps and original units. Check that power and energy keep their own units.
4. Test native keyboard zoom and source selection, and check what a download actually contains. Log any value that cannot be reached as an unresolved native issue. A static table on this page is not a live test.

Record the Home Assistant and frontend versions, browser, fixture or device, input state, expected result, observed result and where the evidence is kept. Reviewing the source or this page is not a test on a connected device.

For the native definitions, see the Home Assistant documentation for [History](https://www.home-assistant.io/integrations/history/) and the [Statistics graph card](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/statistics-graph/).
